[ga10bprobe3] about-to-read pmu_falcon2_cpuctl reg=0x1710b388 (class=pmu-falcon2) — if this is the LAST line, THAT read was EL3-fatal and the boot ended inside it
[ga10bprobe3] pmu_falcon2_cpuctl @0x10b388 = 0x00000010 expect=halted bit4 — the PMU is a SECOND engine; NEW aperture, read LAST by design
[ga10bprobe3] pmu_falcon2_cpuctl decode: halted(bit4)=1 — the PMU engine's own halt state
[ga10bprobe3] bcr_dmacfg lock_locked=0 (raw=0x00000000) — 1 means the BCR is locked for this power cycle and rung 4 CANNOT reprogram it without a cold boot
[ga10bprobe3] opt_wpr_enabled=0x00000001
[ga10bprobe3] pg=0x1 clk=2/3 regs=16 of 25 readable, 9 UNREADABLE -> COMPLETE
[ga10bprobe3b] rung 3b — GSP engine reset (assert -> hold -> deassert) then, only if the readback is sane, ONE MAILBOX0 scratch write. Verdict vocabulary: MAILBOX-HELD | MAILBOX-MISMATCH | MAILBOX-SKIPPED reason=<cpuctl-all-ones|cpuctl-pri-error>
[ga10bprobe3b] address class gsp-falcon-engine (a KNOWN aperture, but a NEW ACCESS KIND: BAR0=0x17000000, pgsp_falcon_engine at 0x171103c0) — the module's first write_volatile to a GA10B register
[ga10bprobe3b] about-to-WRITE pgsp_falcon_engine reg=0x171103c0 val=0x00000001 (engine reset ASSERT, bit0=1) — if this is the LAST line, THAT WRITE was fatal and the boot ended inside it
[ga10bprobe3b] assert held >= 1 ms (facts require >= 10 us)
[ga10bprobe3b] about-to-WRITE pgsp_falcon_engine reg=0x171103c0 val=0x00000000 (engine reset DEASSERT) — if this is the LAST line, THAT WRITE was fatal and the boot ended inside it
[ga10bprobe3b] about-to-read priscv_cpuctl reg=0x17111388 (post-reset readback; rung 1 measured 0x10 = halted before any reset ever ran) — if this is the LAST line, THAT read was EL3-fatal
[ga10bprobe3b] priscv_cpuctl @0x111388 = 0x00000010 halted(bit4)=1 — sane, so the MAILBOX write is authorised
[ga10bprobe3b] about-to-WRITE gsp_falcon_mailbox0 reg=0x17110040 val=0x5a5aa5a5 — POINTER IS PUBLIC-RECALLED (nouveau nvkm/falcon; open-gpu-kernel-modules dev_falcon_v4.h; both MIT), NOT from the ACKED facts file: falcon-base+0x040, corroborated only by that file's matching v1 offsets. If this is the LAST line, THAT WRITE was fatal and the boot ended inside it
[ga10bprobe3b] about-to-read gsp_falcon_mailbox0 reg=0x17110040 (the scratch readback) — if this is the LAST line, THAT read was EL3-fatal
[ga10bprobe3b] mailbox0 wrote=0x5a5aa5a5 read=0x5a5aa5a5
[ga10bprobe3b] -> MAILBOX-HELD — a GA10B engine register accepted a write from this kernel and held it; the CCPLEX can drive this engine's scratch state with the GSP halted
[ga10bprobe3b] rung 3b complete
[ga10bprobe3] clk 41 DISABLE (restore) err=0
[ga10bprobe3] clk 304 DISABLE (restore) err=0
[ga10bprobe3] restored: pg=0x1 (was 1) clocks-disabled=2 of 2 enabled here — board left as found (a GSP engine reset, if rung 3b ran, has no restore and needs none: the engine was halted and never-booted before and after)
[ga10bprobe3] rung 3 complete — RETURNING to the boot (no SYSTEM_OFF; the flight is a full boot)
